<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Our origin</span><h1>From Mill Creek to Accra.</h1><p class="lede">A bridge between two communities, built from a simple conviction: where a child begins should never place a ceiling on where they can go.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap grid-2"><img class="story-image" src="assets/images/student-2.jpeg" alt="Students sharing computers during a class in Accra"><div><span class="eyebrow">A personal promise</span><h2>Opportunity changed one life. Now it can open many more.</h2><p>The vision began with the founder’s own journey—from humble beginnings in Mill Creek, Arkansas, to a career in engineering. Limited resources were real, but so were determination, education, community, and the people who chose to believe.</p><p>Technology became a language that could travel: a way to solve problems, create value, and enter rooms that once felt out of reach. In Accra, that experience became a responsibility—to help young people gain access to the same kind of bridge.</p><div class="pull-quote">“We are not deciding what young people can become. We are helping remove the barriers between their talent and their opportunity.”</div></div></div></section>
<section class="section cream"><div class="wrap"><div class="statement"><span class="eyebrow">The idea that moved us</span><h2>Potential grows when it is met with access, belief, training, and opportunity.</h2><p class="lede" style="margin-inline:auto">The emotional spark echoes a theme many recognize from <em>Akeelah and the Bee</em>: extraordinary ability may be present long before the world makes room for it. The learning center is independently inspired by that universal idea and is not affiliated with the film.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap grid-3"><article class="impact-card"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Perseverance</h3><p>We honor the discipline it takes to keep learning when the path is not easy.</p></article><article class="impact-card"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Self-determination</h3><p>Students are creators and decision-makers in their own futures—not passive recipients.</p></article><article class="impact-card"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Community uplift</h3><p>Skills and confidence can ripple outward through families, classrooms, and neighborhoods.</p></article></div></section>
